    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "ok thanks. so if the shipment gets damaged during the ocean transit, since the risk transferred at the port of origin, does that mean the buyer has to handle the insurance claim entirely themselves? or does the seller have some lingering obligation because they were the ones who had to arrange the insurance under CIF?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "While the risk legally transferred to the buyer at the port of origin, the seller has a crucial obligation because they were required to arrange and pay for the insurance under CIF. If damage occurs, the buyer must first file the claim with the insurance provider, but the seller's original policy documentation is essential for this process. Therefore, the seller's role is vital in facilitating the claim, even though the buyer holds the risk.",
      "source": "target",
