    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "that makes sense. one more thing, if the goods are actually lost or stolen from the container while at sea, what kind of documentation should i be looking for to prove the insurance coverage was sufficient? like are there specific certificates or clauses that make a claim easier?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "To prove sufficient insurance coverage for lost or stolen goods at sea, you will need the Marine Insurance Certificate or the policy wording issued by the insurer. Look specifically for clauses detailing \"Institute Cargo Clauses\" (e.g., A, B, or C), as these define what perils—like theft or loss at sea—are covered. Having this original, correctly executed documentation is the primary evidence required by the insurer to process your claim.",
      "source": "target",
